# Decision Intelligence Runtime Variables
# Rename this file to .env on the host machine and replace placeholders.
#
# This template is deliberately tracked in git even though .gitignore ignores `.env*` — it was
# force-added (`git add -f .env.example`) because it is the only written statement of which
# variables the stack needs. Keep it tracked: if it is ever removed from the index, a fresh
# clone or CI checkout gets a stack whose GenAI routes fail closed with nothing explaining why.
# Never put a real value in it.

# Google Gemini API key.
#
# Required by the SERVER-SIDE governed routes:
#   - Campaign Decision Context drafting        /api/v1/campaigns/decision-context/suggest  (ADR-044)
#   - Capability Atlas grounded market research /api/v1/atlas/ask with research enabled     (ATL-06B)
#   - Capability Atlas AI Interpretation        same route, interpretation layer            (ATL-06C)
#
# Server-side only, and the rules are absolute (ADR-044, ADR-049, ADR-055):
#   - it is read from this environment at call time and from nowhere else;
#   - it is NEVER exposed through a NEXT_PUBLIC_* variable — those are inlined into the browser
#     bundle at build time, so naming it that way would publish it;
#   - it is NEVER accepted from a request body, held in client state, or written into source;
#   - it appears in no API response, no capability record, no cache entry and no log or error path.
#
# Behaviour when unset — every governed route fails closed, none fabricates:
#   - the decision-context assistant returns 503 naming this variable and drafts nothing;
#   - Atlas grounded research reports no provider configured and refuses rather than approximating;
#   - Atlas interpretation degrades to the deterministic reading derived from governed records.
# When set, the decision-context route caps how often the key can be spent (per declared tenant +
# origin, and per process) and returns 429 past the cap; the Atlas caps live grounding calls per
# process and caches repeat research questions.
#
# NOTE: the key some users enter in the platform-setup UI is a SEPARATE, legacy mechanism serving
# only /api/ask and /api/briefing. It does not reach any governed server-side route, and setting it
# does not substitute for this variable. See ADR-044 Amendment A.
GEMINI_API_KEY=your_gemini_api_key_here

# Runtime settings
NODE_ENV=production
PORT=3000

# Demonstration auth bypass. Read at BUILD time (Next.js inlines NEXT_PUBLIC_* into the client
# bundle), so setting it at run time alone has no effect on a built image. Defaults to false in
# docker/Dockerfile.web; use docker-compose.local.yml to build a local, bypassed stack. Never
# enable it for a deployed environment.
NEXT_PUBLIC_COGNIX_DEMO_MODE=false
